      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Grand Trunk Western Railroad cut through in 1870, Emmett quickly grew and officially incorporated in 1883.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2025/10/25/history-of-emmett-michigan/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A plain wooden station built at the depot became the bustling hub where farmers, merchants, and tourists gathered.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2025/10/25/history-of-emmett-michigan/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1884 the community erected a large brick Gothic Revival church, a proud landmark that still stands today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://thumbwind.com/2025/10/25/history-of-emmett-michigan/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Emmett Township shares a western border with the city of Battle Creek, linking the two communities.",
